{"reference":"Revelation 13","book":"Revelation","chapter":13,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Beasts and the Number","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The beasts, horns, allotted time, conflict with the saints, and book imagery belong to a pattern of Danielic imagery reused in Revelation in a new literary setting. This helps explain why the chapter presents oppressive power through vivid symbolic figures rather than through ordinary description; the imagery is designed to be read as part of that larger scriptural pattern.","verse_refs":["Revelation 13:1-18"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_013_9affecc1f03773aa57fc4981"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_2","text":"The number is best known as 666, though an ancient textual variant reads 616. A leading, but disputed, explanation calculates “Nero Caesar” through Hebrew letters and accounts for 616 through a different spelling; other explanations remain possible. More broadly, the two beasts portray coercive rule, demanded worship, deception, and exclusion from buying and selling within a symbolic field shaped by Daniel and the Roman world. The chapter does not identify one emperor as its complete key. Its call in verse 10 is for endurance and faithful witness, not for readers to carry out the judgment scenes through religious violence.","verse_refs":["Revelation 13:1-18","Revelation 13:10","Revelation 13:18"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_013_4db45705bc2228543b3444bd"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within Revelation","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"Revelation repeatedly reworks Israel’s Scriptures, including Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. Its seals, trumpets, and bowls also form major sevenfold judgment sequences, with interludes and recurring motifs. Reading chapter 13 within these wider patterns helps place its beast imagery inside the book’s deliberately interconnected symbolic world.","verse_refs":["Revelation 10:1-11","Revelation 11:1-19","Revelation 12:1-17","Revelation 14:1-20","Revelation 15:1-8","Revelation 16:1-21","Revelation 17:1-18","Revelation 18:1-24","Revelation 19:1-21","Revelation 1:1-20","Revelation 20:1-15","Revelation 21:1-27","Revelation 22:1-21","Revelation 2:1-29","Revelation 3:1-22","Revelation 4:1-11","Revelation 5:1-14","Revelation 6:1-17","Revelation 7:1-17","Revelation 8:1-13","Revelation 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_013_1cb14b90316dd1760244e6ad"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}